# React Component Rules

## Structure
- One component per file, named `ComponentName.tsx`.
- Co-locate `ComponentName.css.ts` and `ComponentName.stories.tsx`.
- ≤150 lines; split if larger. Named exports only.

## Props & types
- Explicit `ComponentNameProps` interface above the component.
- Discriminated unions over boolean flags + optional fields.
- `React.forwardRef` for DOM-wrapping primitives.

## Rendering & data
- Data-fetching extracted into `useComponentName` hook; component stays presentational.
- Always handle isLoading / isError / empty states explicitly.
- Subscribe to real-time via a hook; never `new WebSocket()` in a component.
- Lazy-load page-level components: `React.lazy` + `Suspense` + skeleton fallback.

## Styling (vanilla-extract)
- Sibling `.css.ts` file. Pull every value from `@app/design-tokens`.
- Themes via `createTheme` + `themeContract`. Responsive: `@media` inside `.css.ts`.

## Stories
- Every shared `packages/ui` component: default + variants + loading + error + empty.
